@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "how to rip lips";
}

<div class="text-start">

  <div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="row g-4 align-items-center">
      
      <!-- Left: Card -->
      <div class="col-12 col-md-auto">
        <div class="card" style="width: 18rem;">
          <img src="~/img/fishing3.jpg" class="card-img-top" alt="person holding a large bluegill">
          <div class="card-body">
            <label class="card-title" for="hours">How many hours you want to fish with me?</label>
            <input class="form-control mt-2" id="hours" type="number" />
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-dark w-100" id="calculate">calculate cost</button>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <label class="card-title">Cost of fishing trip</label>
            <p class="card-text mt-1 mb-0" id="cost">$0.00</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: Text -->
      <div class="col-12 col-md">
        <h1 class="display-4">how to catch hogs</h1>
        <p>
          A day on the river or lake with me is simple: we show up, get set up fast, and start catching fish.
          You don’t need to bring anything except whatever snacks or drinks you want. I’ve got the rods, reels,
          tackle, and the game plan. I’ll ask what you’re hoping to catch (or what you want to learn), then we’ll
          pick the best spot based on the conditions that day.
        </p>

        <p>
          Once we’re on the water, I’ll walk you through the basics—casting, retrieving, how to set the hook, and
          what to look for so you’re not just “fishing,” you’re actually targeting fish. If you’re new, I’ll keep it
          easy and focus on building confidence. If you’ve fished before, we’ll level it up: reading structure,
          dialing in depth, and switching baits or presentations until we find what they want.
        </p>

        <p>
          I handle the technical stuff: tying knots, changing lures, adjusting your drag, and picking the right
          technique for the moment. I’ll also teach you why we’re doing what we’re doing—so by the end you’ll
          know how to repeat it on your own. And if we hook into a good one, I’ll help you land it, take a quick
          photo, and get it back in the water safely.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
          The goal is for you to have a fun, relaxed day and leave with real skills—not just stories. Whether we’re
          chasing big bites or steady action, we’ll keep moving, keep learning, and make the most of the time on
          the water.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
